fig('Current support planner: retain an allowed fallback','The planner chooses an action; a separate generator writes the selected message.','08-guarded-planner','A proposal replaces the baseline only when the replacement conditions pass.',[13,14], 'A = deterministic event rule. Replacement requires a valid permitted proposal, analytic support and a predicted gain of at least 0.04.')
tbl('Why reject-only verification was not retained','The earlier designs changed action selection while keeping shared permission constraints.',[
 ['Design','What it adds','Problem exposed'],['Fixed rules A','Choose a baseline action','Limited flexibility, but a useful control'],['Model proposal + lookahead','Propose and score possible actions','More stages did not beat A on utility in that fold'],['Reject-only verifier','Reject the selected proposal','Can remove a usable action without replacing it'],['Guarded replacement H','Keep A unless a proposal qualifies','Retains an allowed fallback when a proposal fails']], 'Preserve a usable baseline instead of treating rejection as a better action.',[13,14,15], 'Utility, preferred-action agreement and action validity are different measures. An earlier label/validity interpretation was corrected.')
